<Victor_Hugo> <base.kwebbase.kwtopic.has_sentences> "Late that year Victor finished his most famous novel of all: \'The Hunchback of Notre Dame.\' In 1832 the family moved upmarket, to 6, Palais Royale,  into sumptuous surroundings,  where Victor played host to such notables as the Polish composer Liszt In 1833 Victor fell for 26-year-old Juliette Drouet,  a beautiful actress who had appeared in one of his plays, and he,  Adele and Juliette set up a ménage a trios." .
